# Patch for issue #278 phase 2 (Factory side): a tenth policy check kind,
# `check: metric`, amending ADR 0004's check vocabulary.
#
# One file diff, path relative to the company root:
#   .specs/adr/0004-policy-controls.md -- bumps the Status line and adds
#     amendment 10, recording the new `check: metric` kind, its fields,
#     its judgement (shared with Quality's own metric measure), the
#     families it refuses as circular, and why: scope-reported metrics
#     (#278, phase 1) needed a way to close an L6 control.
#
# This repository (`projects/factory`) does not own `.specs/`; the ADR
# lives in the company root (`business-factory`). Apply from there with:
#   patch -p1 < 278-adr-0004-metric-check.patch
--- a/.specs/adr/0004-policy-controls.md	2026-10-05 23:38:57
+++ b/.specs/adr/0004-policy-controls.md	2026-10-05 23:39:19
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 # ADR 0004: Policies as a control catalogue checked against evidence

-- Status: Accepted, amended 2026-10-04 to name the evidence channel (see
-  "Amendments" at the end)
+- Status: Accepted, amended 2026-10-04 to name the evidence channel and
+  2026-10-05 to add a `metric` check kind (see "Amendments" at the end)
 - Date: 2026-09-24
 - Decision owners: Business Factory
 - Tracking: https://github.com/ingo-eichhorst/factory/issues/74
@@ -266,3 +266,29 @@
    are still being migrated in #193; accepting the rule does not assert
    those steps are finished. Persisting the facts a decision acted on is
    deferred to a separate ADR, without removing existing audit records.
+10. **A tenth check, `metric`,** was added on 2026-10-05
+    (https://github.com/ingo-eichhorst/factory/issues/278, phase 2) once a
+    scope could declare its own reported metrics (phase 1, same issue):
+    without it, that progress could show at L5 Improvement but never close
+    an L6 control. `{ check: metric, metric, above, below, max_age }` names
+    a metric -- a scope's own `reported.<source>.<metric>` or a built-in
+    one -- held to inclusive `above`/`below` bounds and a freshness
+    `max_age`, judged by the exact same arithmetic a Quality
+    `measure: { metric, above, below, max_age }` already uses (one shared
+    function, `factory_assurance::metrics::judge_metric`, so the two kinds
+    of authored catalogue can never drift apart on what "met" or "stale"
+    means). Unlike Quality's four-way status, a control only ever reads
+    `met` as `satisfied`: `not_met`, `stale` and no value at all are all
+    `open`, with the reason -- the status vocabulary above has no bucket of
+    its own for "used to be current" or "found but wrong", and this
+    amendment does not add one. `compliance.<framework>`,
+    `open_controls.<framework>` and `quality.<characteristic>` are refused
+    on this check as circular -- a control judged by a number this same
+    evaluation produces would never be a measurement -- the same reasoning
+    Quality already applies to its own `quality.*` measures; refused both
+    as a catalogue finding when the file loads and again, defensively, if
+    one survives into evaluation anyway. An unknown metric id is a finding
+    too, the same treatment an unknown `daemon` fact or `secrets` location
+    already gets. This is a new evidence kind, so it amends this ADR's
+    check vocabulary; it changes no existing check's meaning, freshness
+    rule, status or rollup.
